title: '''docs/README.org'' opens with a plea for an algebra, a meditation and "Skg is only currently useable with the help of AI", and says what skg is only at its 33rd line.'
pid: 3e3a84c1-48b0-40b4-8bd3-96779a29f063
body: |2-
  The fourth heading tells the reader, who has no AI, to "Just ask for
  this", above questions it does not answer ("How do I make a node?",
  "Save?", "Fork?"). A reader who takes it at its word stops here;
  one who reads on finds what skg is after a page of things that are
  not. What a thing is for should come before the rest (c), and what
  is not written yet said in the first person (f).
  Change: open with what skg is, the pitch, setup, the commands and the
  data model; then the honest limit in Jeff's voice ("I have not yet
  written a page that takes you from installing skg to a first note"),
  with each of those questions linked to the page that answers it or
  marked as not answered anywhere; the algebra, the meditation and
  "to understand the code" last. ("whateer" is a typo for "whatever".)
